request:
thirty seconds, and ID 0 to mean "pick an id for me"

POST /v3/lease/grant
{
  "ID": "0",
  "TTL": "30"
}

response:
the id the store picked and the TTL it settled on, both as strings

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "ID": "3758430593072193541",
  "TTL": "30",
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "1272238390118111867",
    "member_id": "3094728604395025448",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "1"
  }
}

request:
a point read of a key that was written with a lease attached

POST /v3/kv/range
{
  "key": "bGs="
}

response:
the usual kv, plus `lease` naming the lease that owns it

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "count": "1",
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "1867879645637595737",
    "member_id": "14574022099556372145",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "2"
  },
  "kvs": [
    {
      "create_revision": "2",
      "key": "bGs=",
      "lease": "4242",
      "mod_revision": "2",
      "value": "YWxpdmU=",
      "version": "1"
    }
  ]
}
